<title>FINLAND: ENSO, NESTE SET MALAYSIAN J/V.</title>
<headline>ENSO, NESTE SET MALAYSIAN J/V.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish forestry group Enso Oy said in a statement on Wednesday it would set up a joint-venture with Finnish energy group Neste Oy in Malaysia to produce phonolic resin impregnated overlaying films.</p>
<p>The companies will invest $14 million in total in the company, of which Enso will hold 70 percent and Neste 30 percent, Enso said.</p>
<p>&quot;Neste will contribute know-how in resins, while (Enso) Laminating Papers has the paper and impregnating expertise,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Enso said the main supplier of would be the German company Vits Machinenbau GmbH.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0248</p>
